-- a byte string as a code (so that a term holding one quotes, and the specializer's normal form
-- of a program over a fresh buffer exists): the fresh string of its length, then a store per
-- nonzero 8-byte word (and a 4-byte store for a tail, overlapping the last word when needed),
-- each with the buffer's length as the access codes carry it (lib/code.cub: class 6 %bytes, class 4
-- the stores); a string shorter than 4 bytes quotes only when empty
q-bytes v n =
  if %weq n #0 then some (cprim #1536 (lcons (cwlit #0) lnil))
  else if %wlt n #4 then none
  else some (q-bytes-go v n #0 (cprim #1536 (lcons (cwlit n) lnil)))
